{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BringsSurface.SwClassicalJetExactness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BringsSurface.SwClassicalJetExactness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneC8SuperExpBound"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.classical_jet_period_ne_lw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.classical_jet_period_ne_lw","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/sw-classical-jet-exactness.lean#L110-L128","doc":"**The classical-jet period cannot be the binding period.** The classical\nbinding period `a_D^{(m)} = lw(m−1) = I(m)/m` is nonzero for `m ≥ 1`, while the\nclassical-jet period is identically zero — so the classical-jet reading of the\nidentification `a_D^{(n)} = ∮ λ_SW^{(n)}` fails on every cycle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.involutionNumber_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.involutionNumber_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/sw-classical-jet-exactness.lean#L95-L108","doc":"`I(m) ≠ 0` for the involution numbers (ℕ-valued form of the library lemma\n`QOU.BraidKnot.YoungTableauStandard.involutionNumber_pos`; restated here so the\ncontent-block sibling does not pull that module's dependency cone). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.classical_jet_period_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.classical_jet_period_zero","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/sw-classical-jet-exactness.lean#L81-L93","doc":"**Exactness kills the classical-jet period.** If the period is `2πi` times\nthe residue sum (`prop:sw-period-residue-sum`, hypothesis `hperiod`) and every\nlocal residue is that of a positive-order classical jet (`hres` — the local\nface of `λ_SW^{(n+1)} = d(X^{(n)})`), the period vanishes. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:sw-classical-jet-exactness","label":"prop:sw-classical-jet-exactness","md":"quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/sw-classical-jet-exactness.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.fresidue_jet_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.fresidue_jet_succ","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/sw-classical-jet-exactness.lean#L74-L77","doc":"Every positive-order classical jet is exact — `jet X (n+1) = fderiv (jet X n)`\nis a derivative — so its residue vanishes at every point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.jet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.jet","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/sw-classical-jet-exactness.lean#L68-L72","doc":"The `n`-th classical jet of a local expansion: `n`-fold termwise derivative\n(the coefficient-level face of `X^{(n)} = dⁿX/dzⁿ` on the curve). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.fresidue_fderiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.fresidue_fderiv","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/sw-classical-jet-exactness.lean#L61-L66","doc":"**The residue of an exact form vanishes**: the `t⁻¹` coefficient of a\ntermwise derivative is `((−1)+1)·f(0) = 0`. This is the invariant behind the\n(b)-exclusion: `d(anything)` has no residue, anywhere, ever. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.fderiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.fderiv","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/sw-classical-jet-exactness.lean#L57-L59","doc":"Termwise derivative of a formal Laurent expansion:\n`(Σ c_e tᵉ)' = Σ (e+1)·c_{e+1} tᵉ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Brings.fresidue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Brings.fresidue","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/sw-classical-jet-exactness.lean#L53-L55","doc":"Formal residue of a local Laurent expansion, presented as its coefficient\nfunction `f : ℤ → R`: the coefficient of `t⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}